{"id": 10009441, "reference": "A12/01435/23", "publication_date": "2023-06-28T19:34:34.187Z", "modification_date": "2023-06-28T19:34:34.189Z", "country": "Sweden", "product_category": "ELECTRICAL_APPLIANCES", "product_name": "Electric fly trap", "product_name_specific": " Flytrap Insektslösa Roterande Fällor", "risk_description": "Solders on connection to battery and on the charger have excessive concentrations of lead and cadmium (measured values up to 84.6% and 0.11% by weight, respectively).\nLead poses a risk to the environment. Cadmium bio-accumulates and poses a risk to the environment.\n\nThe plastic material in the cable has excessive concentrations of bis(2-ethylhexyl) phthalate (DEHP) and short chain chlorinated paraffins (SCCPs) (measured values up to 0.97%  and 2.9% by weight, respectively). \nDEHP may harm the health by causing possible damage to the reproductive system.\nSCCPs persist in the environment, are toxic to aquatic organisms at low concentrations and bio-accumulate in wildlife and humans, posing a risk to human health and the environment. Prolonged exposure to them through the skin may cause cancer.\n\n", "legal_provision": "The product does not comply with the requirements of the Directive on the restriction of the use substances in electrical and electronic equipment (RoHS 2 Directive) nor with the Persistent Organic Pollutants (POP) Regulation. ", "country_of_origin": "People's Republic of China", "sold_online": "YES", "notification_type": "ARTICLE_12", "brands": ["Flytrap"], "model_types": [], "risk_types": ["CHEMICAL", "ENVIRONMENT"], "measures": ["PRODUCT_WITHDRAWAL_FROM_MARKET"], "embedding_model": "siglip2-b16-256", "embedding_dim": 768, "photos": [{"photo_id": 10086784, "main": true, "embedding": ""}, {"photo_id": 10086785, "main": false, "embedding": ""}]}